# Accessibility

Every component, layout, and interaction we design or implement must be usable with keyboard, screen reader, and visible focus — not mouse/hover only.

## Required

- **Keyboard:** Tab/Shift+Tab through all controls. Enter/Space activate. Escape closes menus, dialogs, and overlays and returns focus to the trigger. Arrow keys move within `role="menu"` lists.
- **Visible focus:** `:focus-visible` must be as clear as hover. Never `outline: none` without a replacement. Prefer the Figma hover wash plus inset (nav lists: 4px pad, item fills the cell). Pills/buttons use `outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus)` (`--c` / `#BBCAC5`) and `outline-offset: 2px`.
- **Do not** put hover styles only inside `@media (hover: hover)` without a matching `:focus-visible` rule.
- **Names:** Icon-only controls need `aria-label`. Menus need `aria-expanded`, `aria-haspopup`, and `aria-controls`.
- **Motion:** Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not convey state with animation or color alone.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — keyboard user sees nothing */
.item:hover { background: var(--e); }
.item:focus { outline: none; }

/* ✅ GOOD — hover and keyboard share the same language */
.item:hover,
.item:focus-visible {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--e) 30%, transparent);
}
```

Before calling UI done, Tab through the changed control and confirm the focused item is obvious.
